{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 671 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "e524f038f4b5692de7561a2177427129cffb3767c704b4365309d499addccb53" :edb/db-before-t 670 :edb/db-after-t 671 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533983 50 #inst "2026-10-05T23:50:39.324Z" 13194139533983 true] [17592186083149 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275756 13194139533983 true] [17592186083150 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275743 13194139533983 true] [17592186083150 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275749 13194139533983 true] [17592186083151 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275736 13194139533983 true] [17592186083151 1020 #edb/ref 17592186275746 13194139533983 true] [17592186275736 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275737 13194139533983 true] [17592186275736 1089 "q-170502" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275736 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533983 true] [17592186275736 1100 "Factor $4{w}^{4}+36{w}^{2}+81.$" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275736 1113 #uuid "d10758e2-afad-59fb-a650-755ee75719ab" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275736 1145 "First, let's factor the expression as a perfect square trinomial in ${w}^{2}.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{w}^{4}+36{w}^{2}+81 & ={(2{w}^{2})}^{2}+2\\cdot (2{w}^{2})\\cdot 9+{9}^{2} \\\\  & =(2{w}^{2}+9)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to factor the sum of squares in the parentheses. To do this, we first write it as a difference. Then, we rewrite the second term using ${\\text{i}}^{2}=-1.$ Finally, we factor as a difference of squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{w}^{2}+9 & =2{w}^{2}-(-9) \\\\  & =2{w}^{2}-(9{\\text{i}}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\sqrt{2}w)^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2} \\\\  & =(\\sqrt{2}w+3\\text{i})(\\sqrt{2}w-3\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this back into our main expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{w}^{4}+36{w}^{2}+81 & =(2{w}^{2}+9)^{2} \\\\  & =((\\sqrt{2}w+3\\text{i})(\\sqrt{2}w-3\\text{i}))^{2} \\\\  & =(\\sqrt{2}w+3\\text{i})^{2}(\\sqrt{2}w-3\\text{i})^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275737 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275738 13194139533983 true] [1759218627