an imaginary number. Use $i$ to denote the imaginary unit.\n\n$-12{t}^{2}-108=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275743 1113 #uuid "f99c5aa8-3278-5c9d-822e-715dedb6f9c1" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275743 1145 "First, let's factor out $-3$ from the expression:\n\n$$\n-12{t}^{2}-108=-3\\,(4{t}^{2}+36).\n$$\n\nNow focus on factoring $(4{t}^{2}+36).$  \n\nTo factor a sum of squares, we first write it as a difference. Then, we rewrite the second term using ${i}^{2}=-1.$ Finally, we factor it as a difference of squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{t}^{2}+36 & =4{t}^{2}-(-36) \\\\  & =4{t}^{2}-(36{i}^{2}) \\\\  & =(2t)^{2}-(6i)^{2} \\\\  & =(2t+6i)(2t-6i).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting back, we obtain\n\n$$\n-3\\,(4{t}^{2}+36)=-3(2t+6i)(2t-6i).\n$$" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275744 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275745 13194139533983 true] [17592186275744 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533983 true] [17592186275744 1041 "field-1" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275744 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275745 13194139533983 true] [17592186275744 1110 #uuid "2a9d2cef-71b1-5ced-a483-cc981266043a" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275745 1034 "-12(t+3i)(t-3i)" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275745 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533983 true] [17592186275745 1111 #uuid "7dbf3ef3-1509-5a91-80c6-2d11e6eac885" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275746 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275747 13194139533983 true] [17592186275746 1089 "q-367716" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275746 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533983 true] [17592186275746 1100 "Write $81{y}^{4}+72{y}^{2}+16$ in factored form as $(a+bi)^{2}(a-bi)^{2}.$ Use $i$ to denote the imaginary unit.\n\n$81{y}^{4}+72{y}^{2}+16=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275746 1113 #uuid "58e69aa8-4b56-56cf-befa-b88244dc717a" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275746 1145 "First, let's factor the expression as a perfect square trinomial in ${y}^{2}.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}81{y}^{4}+72{y}^{2}+16 & ={(9{y}^{2})}^{2}+2\\cdot (9{y}^{2})\\cdot 4+{4}^{2} \\\\  & ={(9{y}^{2}+4)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to factor the sum of squares in the parentheses. To do this, we first write it as a difference. Then, we rewrite the second term using ${i}^{2}=-1.$ Finally, we factor as a difference of squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{y}^{2}+4 & =9{y}^{2}-(-4) \\\\  & =9{y}^{2}-4({i}^{2}) \\\\  & ={(3y)}^{2}-{(2i)}^{2} \\\\  & =(3y+2i)(3y-2i)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this back into our main expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}81{y}^{4}+72{y}^{2}+16 & ={(9{y}^{2}+4)}^{2} \\\\  & ={((3y+2i)(3y-2i))}^{2} \\\\  & ={(3y+2i)}^{2}{(3y-2i)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275747 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275748 13194139533983 true] [17592186275747 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533983 true] [17592186275747 1041 "field-1" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275747 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275748 13194139533983 true] [17592186275747 1110 #uuid "e4fe303d-c8f6-54f5-bd8d-1dda2971e215" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275748 1034 "(3y+2i)^2(3y-2i)^2" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275748 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533983 true] [17592186275748 1111 #uuid "0c102f60-4f42-52a2-a654-cc1d89d2600c" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275749 1017 #edb/ref 17592186275750 13194139533983 true] [17592186275749 1089 "q-46507" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275749 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533983 true] [17592186275749 1100 "The expression $-100-36{m}^{2}$ is equivalent to" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275749 1113 #uuid "7ce26373-4678-5527-bd99-a2df114e3db9" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275749 1145 "First, let's factor out $-4$ from the expression. We have\n\n$$\n-100-36{m}^{2}=-4(25+9{m}^{2}).\n$$\n\nLet's now focus on factoring the expression $(25+9{m}^{2}).$\n\nTo factor a sum of squares, we first write it as a difference. Then, we rewrite the second term using ${\\text{i}}^{2}=-1.$ Finally, we factor as a difference of squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25+9{m}^{2} & =25-(-9{m}^{2}) \\\\  & =25-(9{\\text{i}}^{2}{m}^{2}) \\\\  & ={5}^{2}-{(3\\text{i}m)}^{2} \\\\  & =(5+3\\text{i}m)(5-3\\text{i}m)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this back into the expression, we get\n\n$$\n-4(25+9{m}^{2})=-4(5+3\\text{i}m)(5-3\\text{i}m).\n$$" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275750 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275751 13194139533983 true] [17592186275750 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275752 13194139533983 true] [17592186275750 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275753 13194139533983 true] [17592186275750 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275754 13194139533983 true] [17592186275750 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275755 13194139533983 true] [17592186275750 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533983 true] [17592186275750 1041 "selection" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275750 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275754 13194139533983 true] [17592186275750 1110 #uuid "f9b8e327-1845-5866-af7f-5a4c46fc9abc" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275751 1034 "-5(3+4\\text{i}m)(3-4\\text{i}m)" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275751 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533983 true] [17592186275751 1111 #uuid "bba9b9ba-4511-5e1d-85fb-1a714da4e619" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275752 1034 "-(5+3\\text{i}m)(5-3\\text{i}m)" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275752 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533983 true] [17592186275752 1111 #uuid "48139f2d-45af-5845-aa6a-640a9edeeb8f" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275753 1034 "-(3+5\\text{i}m)(3-5\\text{i}m)" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275753 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533983 true] [17592186275753 1111 #uuid "a1962e96-7b56-5ef8-a3a7-a8287d02e2cf" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275754 1034 "-4(5+3\\text{i}m)(5-3\\text{i}m)" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275754 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533983 true] [17592186275754 1111 #uuid "0af1d39f-0431-5901-8bbc-118b75f49f7b" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275755 1034 "-5(4+3\\text{i}m)(4-3\\text{i}m)" 13194139533983 true] [17592186275755 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533983 true] [17592186275755 1111 #uuid "c4b5b85b-46b7-5344-8c